  "operative_text": "Section 2 (Minn. Stat. 609.66, subd. 1g(a)): A person who commits either of the following acts is guilty of a felony and may be sentenced to imprisonment for not more than five years or to payment of a fine of not more than $10,000, or both:\nSection 2 (Minn. Stat. 609.66, subd. 1g(a)(2)): possesses a dangerous weapon, ammunition, or explosives in any state building within the Capitol Area described in chapter 15B, other than the National Guard Armory.\nSection 2 (Minn. Stat. 609.66, subd. 1g(b)(2)): persons who carry pistols according to the terms of a permit issued under section 624.714 in a courthouse complex and who so notify the sheriff;\nSection 2 (Minn. Stat. 609.66, subd. 1g(c)): Unless a person is otherwise prohibited or restricted by other law to possess a firearm, the prohibition in paragraph (a), clause (2), does not apply to persons authorized to carry a pistol under section 624.714, while the person is:"
